# Always check out text files with LF line endings, including on Windows (Git for Windows defaults to CRLF).
# afterprompt.sh runs under bash, which fails on CRLF, and Windows users run it from WSL.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Batch files are the exception: cmd.exe is documented to want CRLF, and afterprompt.cmd is the
# Windows front door, so it must not depend on cmd.exe tolerating LF.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.png binary
